Correcting myself on one sentence above, because it was misleading about @alexandre-daubois' second option.

I wrote that resolving in the controller "cannot fix it: the route is static". That is true of the controller alone, but it reads as though the whole option were dead, and it is not. Two things I should have said.

The env placeholder already resolves at runtime in the controller's argument, so the **document** is correct today; it is only the route that is frozen. Verified:

```php
$c->register('svc', ...)->setArguments([['main' => ['resource' => '%env(API_RESOURCE)%', ...]]]);
// resolved at runtime: 'https://api.example.com/api'
```

And the option is reachable, just not by touching the controller alone: `ProtectedResourceMetadataRouteLoader` would declare one dynamic route, `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/{suffix}` with a `.*` requirement and an empty default, and the controller would derive the expected suffix from the resolved identifier and answer 404 on a mismatch. That supports an identifier whose path is unknown until runtime.

I did not take it, for three reasons rather than the one I gave. The collision check between two firewalls moves from build time to runtime: today a shared path throws naming both firewalls, while env-driven paths cannot be compared while the container is built, so one firewall would silently shadow another. A `.*` route also swallows anything else an application puts under that prefix. And `ContainerParametersResource` stops describing what the routes really depend on.

What decided it is that the realistic case is already served. An environment variable interpolated into the URL keeps the path readable at build time and the host resolved at runtime:

```yaml
resource: 'https://%env(API_HOST)%/v1'
```

which routes at `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/v1` and advertises the resolved host. The only thing the refusal loses is an identifier whose path itself is unknown until runtime, which is exactly what a static route cannot serve. I have added that to the description.

If you would rather have the dynamic route, it is about thirty lines across the loader and the controller plus moving the collision check, and I am happy to write it.
